WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:02.800
If you were to ask me what I'm passionate about,

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:07.100
I would probably say something like
physics, or even science communication.

00:00:07.100 --> 00:00:11.260
I would've written that down several times
on something like a scholarship application,

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:16.100
or even just given it as a response when
someone asked me about what I do.

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:21.580
But, I think a lot of the ideas around
finding your passion are very flawed.

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:25.720
So, by all accounts, I guess I'm a very driven person.

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:29.100
I am self-motivated, and I'm interested in lots of things.

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:32.520
I like to achieve things,
and I'm always working on something.

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:35.400
I guess that's just part of my personality,

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:41.840
and what people see of me is that I'm always sort of working on little projects, we're trying to get things done.

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:49.360
So a friend from high school recently said to me,
"Toby, you are so lucky to have found your passion",

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:55.560
and I guess that really got me thinking,
"Am I lucky? Is this really a privileged position

00:00:55.560 --> 00:01:00.880
...that I meant to have found my passion?",
because I don't really see it that way.

00:01:00.880 --> 00:01:08.200
And if we're talking about my passion as being science,
I don't think that's something that, you know,

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:13.000
I was born with as a given passion.
I think that it's something I chose.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:19.320
It's something that I chose to be interested in,
and I chose to pursue, and do things in that area.

00:01:19.320 --> 00:01:25.960
So when my friend said that I was lucky to have
found my passion, she was feeling a lot more down

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:31.760
that she didn't really have anything that she knew
she was really interested in above anything else.

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:36.520
She felt like she didn't have anything
that she was passionate about.

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:42.280
And that's I guess [is] a really hard position to be in– 
to feel like there's something wrong with you

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:46.680
if you don't have one clear direction
that you should be moving in.

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:51.280
And to her, someone like me seems
to have that very clear direction,

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:56.800
and a very definite path to follow,
but that's not the way that I feel.

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:03.600
Yes, I've done a lot of stuff within physics and
science now, but it started off as just an interest,

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:10.400
and aspects of passion grew around
just the years of study and the effort it I've put into

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:16.480
developing this interest in something,
and that's led it to become almost part of my identity,

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:20.520
and my personality is that I'm really into science stuff.

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:25.400
But I don't think, you know, I was born
with some destiny to become a scientist.

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:31.040
I just was interested in something and
chose to make it the path I was going to go down.

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:34.880
I think that your passion is really just a mindset.

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:41.200
And to be honest, if physics, my passion, was to just be deleted from the world one day, just gone,

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:45.920
and I had no longer anything to do with it because it was just gone, I would be okay with that. [R.I.P. Physics]

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:50.480
I'm pretty confident that I would have found 
something else that I was interested in,

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:55.680
that I would have put effort into and pursued,
and that would be my new passion.

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:58.040
I've got interests in a lot of different things.

00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:04.120
Like I said, I guess that's one aspect of
my personality that I easily find things interesting.

00:03:04.120 --> 00:03:09.960
So, if I'd never gone and studied physics, I think
right now, maybe I'd be doing a PhD in something like

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:14.280
psychology, or a field like that,
and I'd be happy with that.

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:18.800
That would be my passion,
and I'd wrap my existence around that new thing.

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:21.720
I don't think there's anything special about physics.

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:26.760
It's just the thing that I happened to 
have chosen in this version of reality.

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:31.120
I guess one thing that was holding my friend
back from pursuing things a bit more

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:36.960
was that she felt like she hadn't been
lucky enough to just be handed a passion.

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:40.680
But I think another aspect of it is a fear of failure.

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:44.520
So the same person said to me
that they do fear trying new things

00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:49.240
because they do have a fear of failure,
and that's really common.

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:55.600
It is tied up with a lot of insecurities about everything, and it can really prevent you from trying new things,

00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:59.080
and from selecting an interest to become your passion.

00:03:59.080 --> 00:04:02.720
For example, I've never thought that
I was the best at something like physics,

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:05.520
I never thought that I was the very best at it,

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:08.440
and even something like making videos for YouTube.

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:12.600
I look back at videos that I only made
a week ago and will cringe at them.

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:18.680
But...if I was waiting to feel really secure about everything that I did and everything that I made,

00:04:18.680 --> 00:04:25.400
I would never have made a single video ever, and it's likewise I probably would never have pursued physics.

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:32.080
If I'd allowed myself to be afraid of
not being as good as someone else?

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:39.200
Guess what I did was just accepted that there's a transition of trying and not being so great at something,

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:43.240
and I was able to find a mindset
where that didn't bother me.

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:47.080
I can't say that I've always been
able to find that mindset.

00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:52.120
I've had things that I was insecure about
that I did let consume me sometimes,

00:04:52.120 --> 00:04:57.840
but I saw the importance of finding that 
mindset where you aren't afraid of failure.

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:04.200
Because, I guess, if you're going to try and pull
yourself out of that spot where nothing interests you,

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:08.440
you have no passions and you don't know how to
find one because just nothing is interesting.

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:13.760
I guess it's all about trying to overcome
the fear of failure and trying new things,

00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:18.080
trying skill based activities,
and developing your skills in them.

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:25.840
Passions are all about the situation you've been placed in throughout your childhood, the activities you've tried,

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:30.000
and the things that you've just been able
to have a go at and develop skills in.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:33.460
Because once you develop skills in something
and you start to become good at it,

00:05:33.460 --> 00:05:36.720
I think it naturally makes you like that thing more,

00:05:36.720 --> 00:05:41.320
and that might develop them to the
one thing that you would call your passion.

00:05:41.320 --> 00:05:44.800
I think a passion really just means
the thing that you do the most,

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:48.160
and often that's something you're good at,
something that you're trying out,

00:05:48.160 --> 00:05:50.480
something you're trying to become better in.

00:05:50.480 --> 00:05:52.960
I do think that I am lucky in a way,

00:05:52.960 --> 00:05:58.280
thinking back to the comment that my friend made,
but not lucky to have found my passion.

00:05:58.280 --> 00:06:03.520
I still don't believe that there's any God giving out passions or gifts when you're born.

00:06:03.520 --> 00:06:09.680
It's not like each human has some passion
deep down in their code that you have to unearth.

00:06:09.680 --> 00:06:12.200
It's just the places that we fall into.

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:18.820
I do feel lucky that I had a mindset
where I found things interesting,

00:06:18.820 --> 00:06:25.280
and that has defined who I am. It's to find the fact
that when trying to select something to pursue,

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:31.240
I felt like I had multiple options. And if one of them
was to go away, like physics was to just disappear,

00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:37.020
I would be just fine with that. 
In fact, I often think about the version of myself

00:06:37.020 --> 00:06:40.180
that did pursue something different,
like psychology or philosophy.

00:06:40.180 --> 00:06:42.900
Those are some of the other things I'm interested in.

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:46.920
And you know, I would have just put
all my effort into that other thing.

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:54.140
So I do feel lucky in that way, and I guess my advice [is]
if you don't feel like you have that ability to find

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:59.980
lots of things interesting is to just try as many
skill based activities as you can.

00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:04.120
